    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (72.87) and **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) leading the charge as our most efficient starts. **Corbin Carroll** finds himself in a high-leverage spot against Wrobleski; the combination of a favorable SP_xERA and a slow delivery from the opposition creates an optimal environment for his elite speed to influence the SB category. Meanwhile, **Isaac Paredes** benefits from the highest SP Skill boost of the day (19%) against a vulnerable V\u00e1squez, making him an essential anchor in the middle of our lineup. **Mickey Moniak** (71.00) also deserves a high-leverage tag, as his strong platoon advantage (14%) against a right-handed matchup elevates his profile significantly above the rest of the outfield.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Cole Young** (42.59), who remained on the bench despite a favorable order placement. While **Cole Young** possesses the sprint speed we crave to address our scarcity in SB, his underlying efficiency metrics against a tough matchup with Seymour were edged out by the superior park and platoon profiles of players like **Max Muncy** and **Henry Bolte**. Speaking of the outfield, we are leaning heavily into the matchup against Miller, who carries an xERA of 3.53 but is being neutralized by favorable winds, giving **Henry Bolte** and **Tyler Soderstrom** a meaningful bump in their scoring output. **Josh Naylor** and **Austin Riley** remain our primary concerns; both are flirting with the lower end of our starting floor due to poor SP_xERA matchups (3.37 and 2.91, respectively), and we will need them to overcome these elite arms to maintain our Roto consistency.",
